   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Fund to Fight AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To substantially reduce the burden of TB in Mauritania by 2018 - Mauritania (01-Jul-2016-30-Jun-2019)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mauritania, Tuberculosis, National Executive Secretariat for the Fight Against AIDS of the Islamic Republic of Mauritania (SENLS Mauritania)This program has the following goals: To substantially reduce the burden of TB in Mauritania by 2018 in line with the objectives of the global strategy for tuberculosis prevention, care and control after 2015. The objectives of this program are: To detect 12,137 cases of TB by 2018..  To diagnose and treat 181 cases of MDR-TB between 2015 and 2018..  To increase the demand for TB care and treatment..  To strengthen the program&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122;s capacities..  To strengthen the program&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122;s M&amp;E system and promote research..  To successfully treat at least 85 percent of new bacteriologically confirmed TB cases by 2018.  To test at least 90 percent of notified TB cases for HIV and ensure a treatment success rate of 80 percent of TB/HIV co-infected patients by 2018.</narrative>
  </description>
